Implement GoldenValue as a frozen dataclass in base.py:

@dataclass(frozen=True)
class GoldenValue:
    value: float
    unit_precision: str  # 'millions', 'thousands', 'exact'
    source_url: str      # EDGAR filing URL
    accession: str
    page_or_note: str    # 'p.45' or 'Note 12'

    @property
    def tolerance(self) -> float:
        if self.unit_precision == 'millions':
            return 0.5e6
        elif self.unit_precision == 'thousands':
            return 0.5e3
        else:  # exact
            return abs(self.value) * 1e-9

Add validation to ensure unit_precision is one of the allowed values and source_url/accession are non-empty.
